/Title (3. If they cannot agree in time, the class abstains. If one representative is unavailable, the other can represent the class.)
/Dest [21 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 1631 0 R
/Prev 1693 0 R
/Next 1668 0 R
>>
endobj
1695 0 obj
<<
/Title (2. The term is one year. There is no limit on re-election.)
/Dest [22 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 1640 0 R
/Prev 1673 0 R
/Next 1696 0 R
>>
endobj
1696 0 obj
<<
/Title (3. If two candidates tie, a run-off is held between them.)
/Dest [22 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 1640 0 R
/Prev 1695 0 R
/Next 1674 0 R
>>
endobj
1697 0 obj
<<
/Title (1. The candidate with the second-highest number of votes becomes Vice-Parliament President and remains a class representative.)
/Dest [22 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 1675 0 R
/Next 1698 0 R
>>
endobj
1698 0 obj
<<
/Title (2. If nobody volunteers to take the minutes, parliament appoints a minute-taker.)
/Dest [22 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 1675 0 R
/Prev 1697 0 R
>>
endobj
1699 0 obj
<<
/Title (2. If the situation does not improve, class representatives mayrequest removal through school leadership. The class representatives then vote on the matter.)
/Dest [22 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 1641 0 R
/Prev 1676 0 R
/Next 1700 0 R
>>
endobj
1700 0 obj
<<
/Title (3. If a two-thirds majority of delegates voting Yes or No supports removal and the SMT agrees, a new election is held.)
/Dest [22 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 1641 0 R
/Prev 1699 0 R
/Next 1677 0 R
>>
endobj
1701 0 obj
<<
